arred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-10-09T19:19:24Z","updated_at":"2015-06-15T20:39:30Z","body":"_Original comment by_ **Jason R. Coombs (BitBucket: [jaraco](http://bitbucket.org/jaraco), GitHub: [jaraco](http://github.com/jaraco))**:\n\n---\n\nThanks for the lead. I'll look into it and provide more detail.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/comments/112203688/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"pytestbot","id":12873537,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODczNTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12873537?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot","html_url":"https://github.com/pytestbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/comments/112203689","html_url":"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/366#issuecomment-112203689","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/366","id":112203689,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDExMjIwMzY4OQ==","user":{"login":"pytestbot","id":12873537,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODczNTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12873537?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot","html_url":"https://github.com/pytestbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-10-10T02:24:09Z","updated_at":"2015-06-15T20:39:30Z","body":"_Original comment by_ **Jason R. Coombs (BitBucket: [jaraco](http://bitbucket.org/jaraco), GitHub: [jaraco](http://github.com/jaraco))**:\n\n---\n\nIn a typical Python environment on Python < 3.3, when a package is loaded from the file system, it has no `__loader__` attribute. In contrast, if the package is loaded from a zip archive, its `__loader__` will be `zipimport.zipimporter`.\n\n`pkg_resources` uses this `__loader__` attribute to determine how to load content from a package. If the loader is not defined, it's treated as None, and `pkg_resources` using the DefaultProvider for serving content from the file system. On Python 3.3, the loader for file-system packages is `_frozen_importlib.SourceFileLoader`, which is also mapped to the DefaultProvider. If the loader is a `zipimport.zipimporter`, a ZipProvider is used instead to provide package resources from a zip file.\n\nWhen pytest patches `__loader__` on the package with an AssertionRewritingHook, however, it is communicating to the environment that AssertionRewritingHook is the class that was used to load that package. Furthermore, when `pkg_resources` attempts to determine how to load content from that package, it doesn't know anything about an AssertionRewritingHook (and probably shouldn't), so falls back to the most naive behavior, the NullProvider.\n\nNext, I'll try to understand better why #317 caused `__loader__` to be set.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/comments/112203689/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"pytestbot","id":12873537,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODczNTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12873537?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot","html_url":"https://github.com/pytestbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/comments/112203691","html_url":"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/366#issuecomment-112203691","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/366","id":112203691,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDExMjIwMzY5MQ==","user":{"login":"pytestbot","id":12873537,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODczNTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12873537?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot","html_url":"https://github.com/pytestbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pytestbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2013-10-10T02:48:09Z","updated_at":"2015-06-15T20:39:31Z","body":"_Original comment by_ **Jason R. Coombs (BitBucket: [jaraco](http://bitbucket.org/jaraco), GitHub: [jaraco](http://github.com/jaraco))**:\n\n---\n\nThe changeset referenced in #317 sets `__loader__` on the module/package. I suspect the fix, then, might be for pytest to register its loader with pkg_resources to use the DefaultProvider. I'll explore that and draft a pull request.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/comments/112203691/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event